[2026-10-26T20:42:19.465Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"reasoning","text":"**Refactoring marker functions**\n\nI'm thinking about how to refactor the marker to return metadata for all markers. I want to use a factory with parameters like `{d, fill, points}`, and ensure the circle path has a circumference of 16. The triangle should return points as well. Using `polygon` just for the marker isn’t ideal, so maybe a helper can return the marker object instead. I also need to adjust how I compute points, especially for circles, ensuring the `markerOutline` function is exported for reuse while keeping the core functionality intact. This approach seems larger but definitely more maintainable.\n**Testing modifications carefully**\n\nI’m thinking that the first step is to test and create modifications using a Python script. I need to proceed with caution to ensure everything works smoothly. It seems wise to set up some initial tests and gather data on the modifications to evaluate their effectiveness. Planning this out properly will help avoid potential issues down the road, so I want to take my time and do it right from the very start!"}}
