[2026-10-26T20:50:16.430Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"reasoning","text":"**Evaluating auto gap settings**\n\nI'm looking at the quality of the default auto gap settings and noticing some issues. It seems like there's an unequal compensation, which extends beyond what's expected, especially with fixed angles. The user likely wants a neater solution. I think I need to manually adjust the symmetry by reducing overlap. The metric shows a current gap of 0.05, so I’ll need to refine that further to achieve the requested spacing between shapes.\n**Refining spacing adjustments**\n\nI'm evaluating the quarter range, which is enough for testing, but the user wants the closest spacing, not just what's available. I need to add a small refinement around the last pass, keeping coordinates within the initial bounds. The current initial values must ensure consistency. I’ll implement candidates within a specific range, adjusting fractions for better alignment. I have to consider penalties for each state, ensuring that changes lead to improvements without causing leaks in previous data.\n**Addressing gap bounds**\n\nI’m working with the gap bounds set between [0,1], and I see that the maximum gap is already defined. I need to handle new cuts properly; they can’t just be hidden away. The default is set to a small value of 4, but I shouldn't set nulls to 0 when the candidate value is at 0. I also want to ensure that there's a way to disable optional fields to prevent any ambiguity, balancing defaults while keeping things explicit."}}
