[2026-10-26T21:16:47.533Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_209","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nroot=Path('docs/case-studies/issue-25')\nfor engine in ('chromium','firefox','webkit'):\n    source=Path('/tmp/issue-25-ci-artifacts')/f'network-{engine}'\n    shutil.copytree(source/'data', root/'data'/'ci-source'/engine, dirs_exist_ok=True)\n    shutil.copytree(source/'screenshots'/'issue25', root/'screenshots'/'ci-source'/engine, dirs_exist_ok=True)\np=root/'README.md'\ns=p.read_text().replace('| 21:05–21:07 |', '| 21:05–21:07 |')\ns=s.replace('Later verification, exact commits', '| 21:07–21:12 | Source CI run 40401691502 passed: 717 unit tests, all three browser engines with the retained 4131-card load, production build and all 120 CV PDFs. Full logs and issue-specific CI captures are archived. |\\\\n| 21:09–21:17 | Installed the remaining pinned local browsers and verified Firefox and Linux WebKit. A bounded pixel probe isolated Linux WebKit antialias quantization at 5°; 2000-pixel sampling retains the same physical tolerance and passes. No application geometry workaround was added. |\\\\n\\\\nLater verification, exact commits')\ns=s.replace(\\\"The browser test rasterizes the actual SVG into a canvas at 1000 pixels and\\\\nmeasures the cyan endpoints independently of the geometry helper. Antialias\\\\ncoverage must count: a narrow tip's last pixel is partially covered, so testing\\\\nonly full-intensity cyan falsely truncates its measured extent. Chromium's\\\\nmeasured endpoints differ by at most one pixel at 5°, 15° and 45°.\\\", \\\"The browser test rasterizes the actual SVG into a canvas at 2000 pixels and\\\\nmeasures the cyan endpoints independently of the geometry helper, with a\\\\ntwo-pixel tolerance (one pixel per 1000 drawing units). Antialias coverage\\\\nmust count: a narrow tip's last pixel is partially covered, so testing only\\\\nfull-intensity cyan falsely truncates its measured extent. Linux WebKit at\\\\n1000 pixels quantizes the 5° tip to a two-pixel discrepancy; at 2000 pixels\\\\nthe difference is one pixel. The bounded [pixel probe](../../../experiments/issue-25-pixels.mjs)\\\\nand [raw coverage rows](data/webkit-pixels.json) preserve this distinction.\\\\nChromium, Firefox and Linux WebKit pass the same normalized tolerance at\\\\n5°, 15° and 45°. CI additionally verifies macOS WebKit.\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=root/'VALIDATION.md'\ns=p.read_text().replace('716 passed before the last zero-gap guard; final full run follows below', '717 passed in source CI; final local run is recorded in all-tests-final.log').replace('[all-tests.log](logs/all-tests.log)', '[final local log](logs/all-tests-final.log), [previous 716-test run](logs/all-tests.log)')\ns=s.replace('[chromium-browser.log](logs/chromium-browser.log), [chromium compatibility run](logs/chromium-browser.log)', '[chromium-editor.log](logs/chromium-editor.log)')\ns=s.replace('Pending final local verification | [log](logs/webkit-browser.log)', 'Pass, including Linux-specific narrow-tip raster measurement | [log](logs/webkit-browser.log), [JSON](data/webkit-browser.json)')\ns=s.replace('The existing editor suite initially wrote \"'`chromium-browser.log`; the later'\"\\\\nissue-specific native-pixel suite uses that filename too. Compatibility\\\\nscreenshots remain under \"'`screenshots/compat-browser`; the next archive revision'\"\\\\nseparates the log names to retain both complete outputs.\\\\n\\\\n', '')\ns=s.replace('is rasterized at 1000 × 1000 pixels.', 'is rasterized at 2000 × 2000 pixels with a two-pixel boundary tolerance,\\\\nequivalent to one pixel per 1000 drawing units. A bounded Linux WebKit probe\\\\nconfirmed antialias quantization at the smaller resolution; the original\\\\nfailure and pixel rows are retained in \"'`webkit-1000px-reproduction.log` and'\"\\\\n\"'`data/webkit-pixels.json`. No application change was needed.'\"')\ns=s.replace('Final status, preserved logs/artifacts and final-head checks will be recorded\\\\nbefore the PR is marked ready.', 'It completed successfully at 21:12 UTC: lint/actionlint, audit, 717 unit tests,\\\\nall five browser suites on Chromium/Firefox/macOS WebKit, the production build\\\\nand 120 CV PDFs passed. See [metadata](data/source-ci.json),\\\\n[complete logs](logs/source-ci.log) and [artifact inventory](data/source-ci-artifacts.json).\\\\nDownloaded browser JSON is preserved under \"'`data/ci-source`, with all'\"\\\\nissue-specific CI screenshots under \"'`screenshots/ci-source`. Complete browser'\"\\\\nartifacts remain linked in the run. The final evidence commit is checked by\\\\nanother fresh run before the PR is marked ready; its URL and exact SHA are\\\\nrecorded in the PR description, avoiding a self-referential archive commit loop.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
